WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.531 --> 00:02.566 align:center line:81%
Thank you, choir, for your testimony.

00:02.599 --> 00:03.867 align:center line:81%
Through that new hymn.

00:04.801 --> 00:06.270 align:center line:81%
The new sacrament hymn,

00:06.270 --> 00:09.706 align:center line:79%
“Bread of Life, Living Water”
fills my soul.

00:10.207 --> 00:14.278 align:center line:79%
One line in the hymn says,
“Now I come before the altar,

00:14.678 --> 00:16.780 align:center line:81%
off’ring Him my broken heart.”

00:17.347 --> 00:19.983 align:center line:79%
My understanding of those words
deepened soon after

00:19.983 --> 00:22.619 align:center line:79%
our family departed
Newbury Park, California,

00:22.819 --> 00:24.688 align:center line:81%
to serve in the Utah Ogden Mission

00:24.688 --> 00:30.460 align:center line:79%
in 2015. I received an invitation to tour
Hill Air Force Base in Layton, Utah.

00:30.994 --> 00:32.796 align:center line:81%
I'd never been on a military base,

00:32.796 --> 00:36.233 align:center line:79%
nor had I met a military
chaplain, or the men and women

00:36.233 --> 00:39.703 align:center line:79%
who work to provide safety
and protection for their country.

00:40.370 --> 00:44.875 align:center line:79%
Chaplain Harp, like thousands of other
voluntary and professional chaplains

00:45.042 --> 00:49.746 align:center line:79%
who serve in our prisons, hospitals,
military installations around the world,

00:49.746 --> 00:51.648 align:center line:81%
inspired and uplifted me.

00:52.149 --> 00:54.785 align:center line:79%
Our last stop on the base
was the sanctuary.

00:55.319 --> 00:59.389 align:center line:79%
I asked the chaplain if he administered
services for all people

00:59.556 --> 01:02.459 align:center line:79%
who desired to ponder,
pray, meditate, and worship.

01:02.859 --> 01:04.761 align:center line:81%
He went to the front wall of the chapel

01:04.761 --> 01:07.864 align:center line:79%
and he pulled a cross
from behind the curtains.

01:08.231 --> 01:11.868 align:center line:79%
He said he used the cross for Protestant
and Catholic services.

01:12.336 --> 01:15.639 align:center line:79%
I asked what he used for our Jewish
brothers and sisters.

01:15.639 --> 01:19.910 align:center line:79%
He went to the other side of the front
wall and he pulled out a Star of David.

01:19.910 --> 01:23.847 align:center line:79%
I then asked, “What do you do
for Latter-day Saint services?”

01:24.414 --> 01:26.149 align:center line:81%
He pushed those symbols away

01:26.149 --> 01:30.287 align:center line:79%
and pointed to the large wooden altar
in the middle of the sanctuary.

01:30.721 --> 01:35.092 align:center line:79%
He said that members of The Church of
Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints prepare

01:35.092 --> 01:37.494 align:center line:79%
and bless the bread
and water on the altar.

01:38.095 --> 01:39.463 align:center line:81%
I asked if the large,

01:39.463 --> 01:44.468 align:center line:79%
seemingly fixed altar was removed
before the services of our Jewish, Muslim,

01:44.468 --> 01:46.903 align:center line:79%
Catholic, or Protestant
brothers and sisters.

01:47.437 --> 01:51.408 align:center line:79%
He said that the altar stays
in place; for several of those faiths

01:51.408 --> 01:53.810 align:center line:81%
also utilize the altar in some way.

01:54.745 --> 01:59.783 align:center line:79%
Abraham built an altar, bound Isaac,
and was ready to sacrifice his only son,

02:00.150 --> 02:04.388 align:center line:79%
but his hand was stayed, and he declared,
like the Lord has declared,

02:04.655 --> 02:08.859 align:center line:79%
“Here am I.” How many times
has the great I Am

02:08.892 --> 02:12.629 align:center line:79%
or one of his prophets
volunteered, “Here am I”?

02:13.330 --> 02:14.831 align:center line:81%
During His Sermon on the Mount,

02:14.831 --> 02:17.634 align:center line:79%
the Savior invited us
to reconcile with our brothers

02:17.634 --> 02:20.437 align:center line:81%
and sisters before we approach the altar.

02:20.904 --> 02:24.474 align:center line:79%
Paul taught that we are “sanctified”
at the altar through the Atonement

02:24.474 --> 02:28.545 align:center line:79%
of Jesus Christ. The prophet Lehi
“left his house ... and his precious

02:28.545 --> 02:30.547 align:center line:81%
things, ... [then] he built an altar ...

02:30.547 --> 02:33.950 align:center line:79%
and made an offering ...
and gave thanks unto the Lord.”

02:33.950 --> 02:38.388 align:center line:79%
The Bible and the Book of Mormon teach us
to worship the Son of God at altars.

02:38.388 --> 02:43.360 align:center line:79%
Why? Our first parents, Adam and Eve,
built and worshiped at altars.

02:43.760 --> 02:44.895 align:center line:81%
After they were cast out

02:44.895 --> 02:48.098 align:center line:79%
of the Garden of Eden
and had worshipped for many days,

02:48.331 --> 02:52.836 align:center line:79%
an angel visited and asked a poignant
question that could be asked of each

02:52.836 --> 02:58.108 align:center line:79%
of us: “Why dost thou offer
sacrifices unto the Lord?”

03:00.977 --> 03:03.180 align:center line:81%
Adam answered, “I know not.”

03:03.780 --> 03:07.617 align:center line:79%
The angel’s response to Adam’s
humble admission is stunning:

03:08.251 --> 03:12.889 align:center line:79%
“This is a similitude of the sacrifice
of the Only Begotten of the Father. ...

03:13.123 --> 03:16.526 align:center line:79%
Wherefore, thou shalt do all
that thou doest in the name of the Son,

03:16.526 --> 03:21.398 align:center line:79%
and thou shalt repent and call upon God
in the name of the Son forevermore.”

03:22.165 --> 03:27.637 align:center line:79%
The sacrament table and temple altars
symbolize the sacrifice of Jesus Christ

03:27.838 --> 03:29.840 align:center line:81%
and His infinite Atonement.

03:30.240 --> 03:32.275 align:center line:81%
As we make and honor our covenants,

03:32.275 --> 03:36.413 align:center line:79%
receiving the ordinances of the sacrament
at church, and the endowment

03:36.413 --> 03:40.117 align:center line:79%
and sealing at the temple,
we bind ourselves to the Savior,

03:40.283 --> 03:43.653 align:center line:79%
gaining greater access
to His mercy, protection,

03:43.754 --> 03:46.356 align:center line:81%
sanctification, healing, and rest.

03:46.957 --> 03:48.391 align:center line:81%
As a 15-year-old young man,

03:48.391 --> 03:52.996 align:center line:79%
I remember asking my dad if I could skip
sacrament meeting—just one Sunday

03:52.996 --> 03:56.399 align:center line:79%
in January—for a special
American football game.

03:56.967 --> 04:00.036 align:center line:79%
He said I was old enough
to make that choice for myself

04:00.036 --> 04:02.672 align:center line:79%
and asked me to consider
one piece of counsel.

04:03.073 --> 04:05.609 align:center line:79%
He said, “If you choose
to miss the sacrament once,

04:05.609 --> 04:08.812 align:center line:79%
it’s much easier
to choose to miss it again.”

04:09.546 --> 04:13.850 align:center line:79%
If the Savior is the great connector,
then the adversary is the separator.

04:14.384 --> 04:18.989 align:center line:79%
He, Satan, tempts us to separate
ourselves from our consecrated places

04:18.989 --> 04:22.559 align:center line:79%
of worship and from
the protection of Jesus Christ.

04:23.193 --> 04:26.096 align:center line:79%
When we worship the Savior,
we receive “power

04:26.096 --> 04:28.732 align:center line:81%
to go against the natural worldly flow.”

04:29.232 --> 04:31.334 align:center line:81%
When we spend time in communion with Him,

04:31.334 --> 04:34.638 align:center line:79%
we have a promise
to be “delivered from Satan.”

04:35.038 --> 04:36.506 align:center line:81%
“Then, as we keep our covenants,

04:36.506 --> 04:39.743 align:center line:79%
He endows us with His ...
strengthening power.”

04:40.210 --> 04:42.946 align:center line:79%
Oh, how I cherish
the experience of communing

04:42.946 --> 04:46.583 align:center line:79%
with the Savior through
covenants made at holy altars.

04:47.217 --> 04:51.488 align:center line:79%
Building an understanding of the Savior’s
eternal Atonement, line upon line,

04:51.555 --> 04:53.089 align:center line:81%
precept upon precept,

04:53.256 --> 04:57.727 align:center line:79%
provides a spiritual inoculation
against the wiles of the adversary.

04:58.295 --> 05:01.865 align:center line:79%
Young Elder Jaggi in Mexico
and Zuster Jaggi in Belgium,

05:01.865 --> 05:05.302 align:center line:79%
and other missionaries
throughout the world are much more likely

05:05.302 --> 05:08.405 align:center line:79%
to see their friends
claim the blessings of baptism

05:08.405 --> 05:10.473 align:center line:81%
and receiving the gift of the Holy Ghost.

05:10.473 --> 05:14.678 align:center line:79%
If their friends attend sacrament
meeting within the first week of contact.

05:15.111 --> 05:16.646 align:center line:81%
A young adult in Tonga

05:16.646 --> 05:19.850 align:center line:79%
or Samoa is much more likely
to be sealed in the house

05:19.850 --> 05:21.952 align:center line:81%
of the Lord if they have prepared for

05:21.952 --> 05:25.488 align:center line:79%
and received their endowment soon
after graduating from school.

05:26.089 --> 05:28.792 align:center line:79%
In the endowment,
members are invited to live,

05:28.825 --> 05:32.229 align:center line:81%
obey, and keep five laws which imbue power

05:32.229 --> 05:36.166 align:center line:79%
and protection. As we make
covenants with the Lord,

05:36.199 --> 05:38.568 align:center line:81%
a reciprocal relationship forms.

05:38.869 --> 05:41.638 align:center line:79%
We demonstrate our loyalty
and love to Him.

05:42.038 --> 05:46.543 align:center line:79%
Our strength and power grow
with each promise made and kept.

05:47.110 --> 05:50.247 align:center line:79%
When we humbly and symbolically kneel
at the altars of the Lord,

05:50.247 --> 05:55.218 align:center line:79%
it’s an opportunity for reflection,
“checked as to the pride of [our] hearts,

05:55.418 --> 05:57.487 align:center line:81%
... [humbling ourselves] before God.”

05:57.487 --> 06:00.090 align:center line:79%
Before going out with
my friends as a youth,

06:00.090 --> 06:04.527 align:center line:79%
my mother would often say, “Remember who
you are, and check in when you get home.”

06:05.228 --> 06:08.732 align:center line:79%
Some nights, I missed my check-in
because I arrived home too late.

06:09.332 --> 06:12.102 align:center line:79%
I regret missing those important
visits with Mom.

06:12.669 --> 06:16.506 align:center line:79%
Today, I look forward to checking
connections with Heavenly Father.

06:16.506 --> 06:18.608 align:center line:81%
In my daily pattern of personal worship,

06:18.608 --> 06:22.178 align:center line:79%
I kneel in prayer next
to my bed or gathered with family,

06:22.178 --> 06:28.051 align:center line:79%
I envision myself kneeling at the altars,
reflecting on, examining my life.

06:28.418 --> 06:32.389 align:center line:79%
I think about the sacrament,
even whole pieces of bread,

06:32.422 --> 06:38.461 align:center line:79%
broken and torn for us,
each a symbol of our Savior's broken body.

06:38.962 --> 06:43.099 align:center line:79%
I’m reminded of President Dallin H. Oaks’
teaching that “each piece

06:43.099 --> 06:48.605 align:center line:79%
of bread is unique, just as the
individuals who partake of it are unique.”

06:49.005 --> 06:53.243 align:center line:79%
When I kneel in prayer,
I think on how I can give God my will.

06:54.044 --> 06:58.348 align:center line:79%
Elder David A. Bednar taught that “the
ordinance of the sacrament is a holy

06:58.348 --> 07:03.687 align:center line:79%
and repeated invitation to repent
sincerely and to be renewed spiritually.

07:04.120 --> 07:08.725 align:center line:79%
The act of partaking of the sacrament,
in and of itself, does not remit sins.

07:08.725 --> 07:11.428 align:center line:81%
But as we prepare conscientiously

07:11.428 --> 07:15.098 align:center line:79%
and participate in this holy ordinance
with a broken heart

07:15.098 --> 07:16.566 align:center line:81%
and a contrite spirit,

07:16.800 --> 07:20.470 align:center line:79%
then the promise is that we may
always have the Spirit of the Lord to be

07:20.470 --> 07:24.007 align:center line:79%
with us. And by the sanctifying
power of the Holy Ghost

07:24.007 --> 07:30.046 align:center line:79%
as our constant companion, we can always
retain a remission of our sins.”

07:30.547 --> 07:36.019 align:center line:79%
When Amy and I look closely
at our life experiences, we celebrate

07:38.088 --> 07:39.689 align:center line:81%
the gift of Jesus Christ’s

07:39.689 --> 07:41.925 align:center line:81%
perfect love and sacrifice.

07:42.158 --> 07:45.628 align:center line:79%
We also see how hell's
fury has been loosed.

07:46.162 --> 07:52.702 align:center line:79%
How can we overcome stares of judgment,
anxiety, depression, cancer, diabetes,

07:52.702 --> 07:57.807 align:center line:79%
online bullying, stolen identity,
lost pregnancies, the loss of a child,

07:57.841 --> 07:59.442 align:center line:81%
a brother, and a father.

07:59.843 --> 08:05.115 align:center line:79%
Because Jesus took the bitter cup
of trembling, the cup of fury—for me,

08:05.215 --> 08:07.617 align:center line:81%
for my family, for all of us!

08:08.018 --> 08:11.054 align:center line:79%
The “bitter cup” he drank
in the Garden of Gethsemane

08:11.054 --> 08:15.158 align:center line:79%
and His suffering “intensified”
on the cross at Calvary

08:15.191 --> 08:20.363 align:center line:79%
allows us to lay the hard,
the insolent, the violent, the furious,

08:20.363 --> 08:23.133 align:center line:79%
and the trembling upon
the altars of the Lord

08:23.133 --> 08:26.202 align:center line:79%
and be “sanctified by the reception
of the Holy Ghost,”

08:26.403 --> 08:29.339 align:center line:81%
always. Sister Patricia Holland said,

08:29.339 --> 08:31.041 align:center line:81%
“My deepest prayer for you

08:31.041 --> 08:34.911 align:center line:79%
and for myself today is that
we will give over completely,

08:34.978 --> 08:38.481 align:center line:79%
lay ourselves at the altar
of God’s promises and peace

08:38.481 --> 08:41.451 align:center line:79%
no matter where we are and no
matter what we have done.”

08:41.951 --> 08:45.121 align:center line:79%
When we come to the altar, we aren’t
earning a reward; we are learning

08:45.121 --> 08:46.456 align:center line:81%
about the Gift Giver.

08:46.790 --> 08:49.659 align:center line:79%
In that learning and covenant
binding comes healing.

08:49.926 --> 08:51.928 align:center line:81%
Nephi said, “He has filled me with his

08:51.928 --> 08:54.964 align:center line:79%
love, even unto the
consuming of my flesh.”

08:55.432 --> 08:57.333 align:center line:81%
And our loving Savior invited,

08:57.333 --> 09:01.704 align:center line:79%
“Will ye not now return unto me,
and repent of your sins, and be converted,

09:01.704 --> 09:04.507 align:center line:79%
that I may heal you?”
When they were little,

09:04.874 --> 09:08.545 align:center line:79%
one of the favorite stories of our two
oldest daughters, Mackenzie and Emma,

09:08.545 --> 09:12.115 align:center line:79%
was “The Chronicles of Narnia: The Lion,
the Witch, and the Wardrobe.”

09:12.315 --> 09:14.951 align:center line:81%
We all fell in love with the lion, Aslan.

09:15.185 --> 09:17.821 align:center line:79%
One of our most memorable
nights reading the book was

09:17.821 --> 09:20.957 align:center line:79%
when the great lion
gave his life for Edmund.

09:21.257 --> 09:22.692 align:center line:81%
Memorable because parents

09:22.692 --> 09:26.096 align:center line:79%
and daughters shed tears
as the lion's life was taken

09:26.096 --> 09:27.864 align:center line:81%
on the Stone Table by the witch.

09:28.231 --> 09:32.235 align:center line:79%
Memorable because hope
persisted, despite the tragedy, until

09:32.235 --> 09:33.870 align:center line:81%
the spectacular happened.

09:34.270 --> 09:38.274 align:center line:79%
Squeals of joy resounded in that little
bedroom when Aslan was resurrected

09:38.274 --> 09:41.911 align:center line:79%
and said, “If the witch knew
the true meaning of sacrifice, ...

09:41.911 --> 09:44.114 align:center line:81%
she would know that if a willing victim

09:44.280 --> 09:47.350 align:center line:79%
who had committed no treachery died
in the traitor's stead,

09:47.350 --> 09:51.421 align:center line:79%
the Stone Table would crack, and death
itself would begin to unwind.”

09:51.788 --> 09:54.157 align:center line:81%
Jesus Christ heals all wounds.

09:54.324 --> 09:57.127 align:center line:79%
Jesus Christ makes it
possible to live again.

09:57.760 --> 10:00.530 align:center line:79%
In his October 2022 general
conference talk,

10:00.763 --> 10:04.134 align:center line:79%
President Russell M. Nelson
described a tour group coming

10:04.134 --> 10:05.635 align:center line:81%
through a temple open house.

10:05.835 --> 10:07.170 align:center line:81%
A young boy was there.

10:07.170 --> 10:10.607 align:center line:79%
He taught: “When the tour
group entered an endowment room,

10:10.607 --> 10:14.277 align:center line:79%
the boy pointed to the altar, where
people kneeled to make covenants with God,

10:14.277 --> 10:16.312 align:center line:81%
and said, ’Oh, that’s nice.

10:16.312 --> 10:20.316 align:center line:79%
Here’s a place for people
to rest on their temple journey.′ ...

10:20.750 --> 10:24.854 align:center line:79%
He likely had no idea about the direct
connection between making a covenant

10:24.854 --> 10:29.692 align:center line:79%
with God in the temple and the Savior’s
stunning promise: “’Come unto me,

10:29.993 --> 10:34.297 align:center line:79%
all ye that labor and are heavy laden,
and I will give you rest.

10:34.564 --> 10:36.599 align:center line:81%
“’Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me;

10:36.599 --> 10:39.369 align:center line:79%
... and ye shall find rest
unto your souls.

10:39.602 --> 10:43.039 align:center line:79%
“’For my yoke is easy,
and my burden is light.’”

10:43.606 --> 10:49.012 align:center line:79%
“The Son of Man has no place to lay
his head,” yet He invited His disciples,

10:49.112 --> 10:53.016 align:center line:79%
you and I, to the sacrament table
to rest with Him there.

10:53.550 --> 10:55.585 align:center line:81%
When “humble souls at altars

10:55.618 --> 10:57.620 align:center line:81%
kneel,” peace abounds.

10:57.854 --> 11:00.523 align:center line:81%
Our Savior’s arms are outstretched;

11:00.857 --> 11:06.696 align:center line:79%
His table is spread. Come
worship the Son of God at His holy altars.

11:06.963 --> 11:08.598 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ,

11:08.598 --> 11:09.599 align:center line:81%
amen.

